{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss","id":1121851,"title":"Dark Eras: The things we miss!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-28T08:02:32-07:00","id":1121851,"title":"Dark Eras: The things we miss!","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I would like to make a list of things that would improve the Dark Eras timelines starting with the things I personally miss the most.<br /> <br /> 1) Historical Weapons / Armor:<br /> I would like to see a table of at least the most common weapons and amor of that time and appropriate stats.<br /> For example even if a weapon exists today an in a certain historical era, the weapons were hardly identical. Not even close. A revolver of the victorian era was much less precise that the versions we have today.<br /> <br /> 2) Travel:<br /> How did people travel during that time? Which travel methods did exist an how common, fast and affordable were they?<br /> <br /> 3) Communication:<br /> How did people communicate at that time? What was already invented? How common and reliable was it? <br /> For example letters, fax, phone...<br /> <br /> 4) Clothing and daily life:<br /> What did people usually wear at that time? Were there class, race or gender differences? What manners and etiquette did exist?<br /> <br /> 5) Other technical devices:<br /> What was already invented and how common and affordable was it?<br /> For example different kind of light sources..<br /> <br /> 6) Medicine:<br /> What wounds, illnesses an diseases could be treated an how?<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe it is just me, but I think, at the moment the published eras do not really lift the amount of research you have to do to play at a specific time. <br /> Adding a small section with the most essential information for that era would really help!<br /> <br /> Right now I want to play in the late victorian era around 1850 to 1900 and endet up buying the last edition of Cthulhu by Gaslight, additionally to Victorian Lost and the Dark Eras books, to find most of the information that I needed. Of course I tried to use Google first, but it was not really helpful. For example you can find out when things are invented, but you rarely find the information about when those things were ready to be sold and how common or affordable they were...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T08:44:49-07:00","id":1121879,"title":"","content":"That's all research you can conduct on your own if you're so interested. Including all that information would've doubled the word-count considering that the book contains dozens of eras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:10:55-07:00","id":1121893,"title":"","content":"I have to disagree with you, OP. The role of a Dark Era for me is to get a sexy, dramatic overview of what makes the period interesting to play in and how it fits into the CofD world; the gritty details of research can easily be done on your own and should be, save for the most evocative bits. Contrast the data-heavy settings from DE1 to the ones that were more flavorful and fun to read.<br /> <br /> Plus, CofD is not GURPS or BRP; knowing how far an individual drachma's worth of spending will get you and other similar fiddly bits just isn't as necessary in a system like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-28-2017, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:15:57-07:00","id":1121897,"title":"","content":"While I agree that one could look up a lot of things, I had no results looking for Neolithic-age names. Clothing, equipment, even sicknesses, all that could be found. But no names. I'm guessing it was due to a lack of proper documentation procedure due to lack of bureaucracy and paper and pen shortages. Even the fiction didn't have a name for the Neolithic Wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-28-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:18:30-07:00","id":1121900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1121893#post1121893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree with you, OP. The role of a Dark Era for me is to get a sexy, dramatic overview of what makes the period interesting to play in and how it fits into the CofD world; the gritty details of research can easily be done on your own and should be, save for the most evocative bits. Contrast the data-heavy settings from DE1 to the ones that were more flavorful and fun to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. There are a lot of details in all eras that can fill libraries. As much as I LOVE all of those details, they aren't all important to eras, nor even desirable if the goal is write something that gets a person excited to play in that time period. Some of the things you meantioned can be useful in some eras, but not all of them. Like, I'd love a Mongol Era about travel, trade, and communication for Geist, but it's a Werewolf era instead, I wouldn't even touch those topics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:24:20-07:00","id":1121903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1121897#post1121897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that one could look up a lot of things, I had no results looking for Neolithic-age names. Clothing, equipment, even sicknesses, all that could be found. But no names. I'm guessing it was due to a lack of proper documentation procedure due to lack of bureaucracy and paper and pen shortages. Even the fiction didn't have a name for the Neolithic Wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're going to, given that the Vinca language remains untranslated. Indeed, the entire literary hypothesis of the era is that the written remains of Vinca are actuallly High Speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:31:49-07:00","id":1121906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1121903#post1121903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you're going to, given that the Vinca language remains untranslated. Indeed, the entire literary hypothesis of the era is that the written remains of Vinca are actuallly High Speech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, which doesn't help. I ended up using deed names. Though one of the werewolves and one of the people had a 'real' name. Lets see. Mages had White Wood, Bee Keeper (can you guess what he does?), Father of Urns, Night Soul, Whispers with Owls, and Drone. There's 26 Drones. Werewolves had Ithka and Empty Heart. And there were a couple regular notable humans, Belo and Noah. And a Nephilim, Holy Gram. Also the Pangaean, Ant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-28-2017, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T02:18:46-07:00","id":1122273,"title":"","content":"I may agree that precise details like clothing or names can be found online - and archaic weapons are in <b>Hurt Locker</b>, for example - but I have to agree with OP we still do not have needed mechanics like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857534-dark-eras-battle-mass-combat-rules\">mass battles</a> or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1070622-dark-eras-other-skills-options\">long sailing</a>. Things that just pop-up in historical RPGs and that letting everything to ST hands sounds a bit <i>too</i> arbitrary. ( 'Who won?' 'Well, they won' 'You are biased ST for NPCs side...' )<br /> <br /> I made fan rules for those to examples, but it should be take for DE 2 corebook first chapter, really. With Eras like War World 1, Missisipi Steamboats or 'Seven Wonders pilgrimage', those things become <i>really</i> important, story wise.<br /> <br /> Or things like how to run literacy/illiteracy or slave/free/noble characters in one group. ( Advise: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-%E2%80%8B-dark-eras-needed-merits\">Use Conditions and Merits</a>. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T03:15:41-07:00","id":1122281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122273#post1122273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">( 'Who won?' 'Well, they won' 'You are biased ST for NPCs side...' )</div> </div> </div> </div>Any mass combat rules they add will be completely inadequet because it wont be able to deal with the insanely varied capabilities that characters and NPCs can possess, meaning that 99% of the game will be unaccounted for in the mass combat rules unless they provide a whole book on Mass Combat. In addition, if you're worried about ST bias... then why are you playing with that storyteller to begin with?<br /> <br /> To be honest, there is more chance of fair result from a storyteller making an informed decision than a set of mechanics in this case simply because of how broad the RPG is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 07-29-2017, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T03:32:56-07:00","id":1122285,"title":"","content":"As I already wrote, I did try to look those thinks up on my own..! Clothes are maybe a bad example, but I would consider them a part of the &quot;essentials&quot; that you need to know to run a game in a certain era.<br /> <br /> I do own Hurt Locker, but as I said, I am not looking for old weapons like bows, but for example an old revolver from 1890. The revolvers today are much more precise. Most weapons of that time didn't even shot straight.. So I can't use those stats.<br /> <br /> For example I tried to find out whether characters could use a phone in their home or at some kind of official station for communication between 1880 and 1900. You can find the date when the technic was invented and &quot;theoretically&quot; usable, but not when it was common and who you could call, and whether it was already available or affordable for the public at all. I can image that it was a small communication system first, maybe connecting the parts of some major cities. But that is just guessing! I can not find any information on that. I wasted(!) a lot of ours on research and have still no satisfying result for even this one point...<br /> <br /> I am not looking for some &quot;large historical text&quot; that would increase the page count tremendously, instead I would prefer a short summary about the most important things you need to know before telling a story during a specific time.<br /> <br /> If you can answer all those &quot;basic questions&quot; after a few minutes of research that's good for you, but I can't. And actually I don't think that those informations would hurt anybody. It just saves time, no matter how you look at it. And in my case a lot of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 07-29-2017, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T06:19:09-07:00","id":1122313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122281#post1122281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any mass combat rules they add will be completely inadequet because it wont be able to deal with the insanely varied capabilities that characters and NPCs can possess, meaning that 99% of the game will be unaccounted for in the mass combat rules unless they provide a whole book on Mass Combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Savage Worlds RPG use rather simple Mass Battle mechanics ( on that I based my fan rules for <b>CoD</b> ) and it works for the numerous of battle scenes in there - and from my play thoughts, it easily works for historical conflicts before WW 1 - I tested it in Vikings Era, I feel it will work for Arthurian times, Pirates Era or (probably) up to Napoleon times.<br /> <br /> In reality, we do not need need very detailed rules - only 'your forces are winning/losing now' and 'actions that PCs can make to work in fight'. My fan rules takes up to one A4 page of text and works fine, in context of most Eras.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122281#post1122281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In addition, if you're worried about ST bias... then why are you playing with that storyteller to begin with?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>I'M A ST </b>in this example - heard those kind of off-screen comments from time to time. Mechanics are for resolving 'outside' situations, were players and ST want to make objective ruling - like hitting the NPCs in combat. Mass Combat is exactly the thing like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T08:05:05-07:00","id":1122340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122313#post1122313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Savage Worlds RPG use rather simple Mass Battle mechanics ( on that I based my fan rules for <b>CoD</b> ) and it works for the numerous of battle scenes in there - and from my play thoughts, it easily works for historical conflicts before WW 1 - I tested it in Vikings Era, I feel it will work for Arthurian times, Pirates Era or (probably) up to Napoleon times.<br /> <br /> In reality, we do not need need very detailed rules - only 'your forces are winning/losing now' and 'actions that PCs can make to work in fight'. My fan rules takes up to one A4 page of text and works fine, in context of most Eras.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>I'M A ST </b>in this example - heard those kind of off-screen comments from time to time. Mechanics are for resolving 'outside' situations, were players and ST want to make objective ruling - like hitting the NPCs in combat. Mass Combat is exactly the thing like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, your rules barely even really take the supernatural into account....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T08:57:02-07:00","id":1122359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122340#post1122340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, your rules barely even really take the supernatural into account....</div> </div> </div> </div>And? It's like saying that historical Medicine Skill variant from <b>Dark Eras</b> 1 corebook is not needed as it not take all possible various healing powers that supernaturals have. ( And almost any supernatural have rules for healing itself. ) In general Mass Combat rules you need only general structure of rules in book - edge cases of each gameline then particular ST will run with each gamelines ideas. Sailing rules do not need anything more than detailed one or two examples rolls.<br /> <br /> BUT those things <i>should</i> be in <b>DE </b>2 corebook, as I mentioned - this kind of things are showing in times of historical game sessions and have story implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T09:41:06-07:00","id":1122372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122285#post1122285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I already wrote, I did try to look those thinks up on my own..! Clothes are maybe a bad example, but I would consider them a part of the &quot;essentials&quot; that you need to know to run a game in a certain era.<br /> <br /> I do own Hurt Locker, but as I said, I am not looking for old weapons like bows, but for example an old revolver from 1890. The revolvers today are much more precise. Most weapons of that time didn't even shot straight.. So I can't use those stats.<br /> <br /> For example I tried to find out whether characters could use a phone in their home or at some kind of official station for communication between 1880 and 1900. You can find the date when the technic was invented and &quot;theoretically&quot; usable, but not when it was common and who you could call, and whether it was already available or affordable for the public at all. I can image that it was a small communication system first, maybe connecting the parts of some major cities. But that is just guessing! I can not find any information on that. I wasted(!) a lot of ours on research and have still no satisfying result for even this one point...<br /> <br /> I am not looking for some &quot;large historical text&quot; that would increase the page count tremendously, instead I would prefer a short summary about the most important things you need to know before telling a story during a specific time.<br /> <br /> If you can answer all those &quot;basic questions&quot; after a few minutes of research that's good for you, but I can't. And actually I don't think that those informations would hurt anybody. It just saves time, no matter how you look at it. And in my case a lot of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it relevant to your story? How does the existence of said devise affects the tale? If favorable, use it, if not there aren't available phones. End of the deal. You don't need to conform to 100% historical accuracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:37:41-07:00","id":1122411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122359#post1122359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And? It's like saying that historical Medicine Skill variant from <b>Dark Eras</b> 1 corebook is not needed as it not take all possible various healing powers that supernaturals have. ( And almost any supernatural have rules for healing itself. ) .</div> </div> </div> </div>No... Since this is Chronicles of Darkness. It'd be ridiculous for werewolves to ignore their abilities in mass combat especially ones like &quot;set a whole region on fire&quot;, and that's one individual. A group of vampires can just obfuscate behind your lines and annihilate you undetected.<br /> <br /> The medicine skill is fine because it doesn't cover anything that isn't mundane. The mass combat rules need to be able to deal with most instanances of mass combat in the game, but chronicles of darkness has enough magic that you have to expect basically all mass combats in such a game will have supernatural elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T15:34:04-07:00","id":1122522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122372#post1122372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it relevant to your story? How does the existence of said devise affects the tale? If favorable, use it, if not there aren't available phones. End of the deal. You don't need to conform to 100% historical accuracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't portrait an era, that I know almost nothing about! I wouldn't even get close! <br /> <br /> In my opinion I should be able to describe the world around them. If I don't know even the basics the world will become very, very weird.. And it's especially weird if you as the storyteller are the only person who knows almost nothing about what's going on at that time... But that's not the point. In my opinion the Dark Eras could(!) offer you a starting point. I was talking about a short summary with the most basic information and nothing more! <br /> The example should only demonstrate how time consuming research can become if you try to look up everything yourself with google. <br /> And whether that knowledge is necessary or not in my case is not for you to decide. Sorry! Everyone should speak for themselves.<br /> <br /> I really get the impression that almost all would hate an overview with some historical basics... Kindly ignoring the fact that it wouldn't hurt them, but help others...<br /> <br /> Nevermind. As I said other systems thankfully did a much better job on that era. So I will use their historical information instead and maybe find a solution for the weapons myself. <br /> I just thought that maybe there are more people besides me who would appreciate the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 07-29-2017, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T19:34:25-07:00","id":1122571,"title":"","content":"I would think the list of inspirational media for each setting would be a good place to start for those kinds of details. Remember also, freelancers aren't necessarily scholars - if you can't google a satisfactory answer there's nothing to say that they could either, especially under common deadline conditions and when the particular thing you want to see has potentially no bearing on the stuff they need to write about with limited words and time.<br /> <br /> I think the thread on resources for Dark Era settings is a great start to fill in those gaps though! Let everyone who finds something interesting, informative, cool, or generally useful add to the pile for everyone else to use if they wish in their own games. That's handy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T19:47:41-07:00","id":1122574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122571#post1122571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think the list of inspirational media for each setting would be a good place to start for those kinds of details. Remember also, freelancers aren't necessarily scholars - if you can't google a satisfactory answer there's nothing to say that they could either, especially under common deadline conditions and when the particular thing you want to see has potentially no bearing on the stuff they need to write about with limited words and time.<br /> <br /> I think the thread on resources for Dark Era settings is a great start to fill in those gaps though! Let everyone who finds something interesting, informative, cool, or generally useful add to the pile for everyone else to use if they wish in their own games. That's handy!</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually started something in another thread not to long ago for online resources. This is a great idea though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T20:19:45-07:00","id":1122580,"title":"","content":"Being slightly more constructive, I actually just found a journal article on Greco-Egyptian names, which could be useful for anything in Ptolemaic Egypt, even those the source data is actually from 100s CE. Gets the idea across though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/view/15293\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://grbs.library.duke.edu/public/journals/11/pageHeaderLogoImage_en_US.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/view/15293\" target=\"_blank\"> Graeco-Egyptian Naming Practices: A Network Perspective | Greek, Roman, and Byzantine Studies </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/view/15293\" target=\"_blank\"> http://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/view/15293 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T03:30:11-07:00","id":1122661,"title":"","content":"Actually that's pretty much what I did, but it was very unsatisfying. First I read a little bit about clothes and that showing the ankle was already considered too much for a woman. And in the next movie and tv series that I watched even upper class women wore dresses that barely hid anything. Maybe books from that time would be a better resource, not just because of accuracy, but also because they name things. When I see a lamp in a movie, I have no idea whether it's an oil lamp or a gas lamp or something else. <br /> And I think it's a very time consuming way to find some useful information. You never know how accurate or typical the things are that you see. A few sentences, that are written in a good resource book, are usually much more informative.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless movies and other media are good as inspirational resources. Even if they are not very accurate they are a good place to start to get a first impression and maybe an idea for the atmosphere.<br /> <br /> You might be right that they can't come up with a summary for every age in a book like Dark Eras, but maybe they do know more about that era than they are writing. Maybe they are using other recourses. We don't know. <br /> I mean other game lines can provide you with historical information and ideas for your game... So it's not impossible.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Collecting resources is actually a really good idea! But maybe we should open another topic for it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T06:05:19-07:00","id":1122677,"title":"","content":"For dress and clothes, remember that social mores varied a lot from time to time, place to place, and class to class, and that what is written down in books saying &quot;this is right and proper&quot; and what was actually DONE may be totally different. If there are hundreds of style articles arguing that dresses shouldn't be longer than X, then you can know for certain that there is a certain society of people around there that the article is responding to. So if it says &quot;ankle is a bit too much&quot;, then you know for certain that there are tons of women who ARE showing ankle. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T10:34:50-07:00","id":1122739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1121851-dark-eras-the-things-we-miss?p=1122677#post1122677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For dress and clothes, remember that social mores varied a lot from time to time, place to place, and class to class, and that what is written down in books saying &quot;this is right and proper&quot; and what was actually DONE may be totally different. If there are hundreds of style articles arguing that dresses shouldn't be longer than X, then you can know for certain that there is a certain society of people around there that the article is responding to. So if it says &quot;ankle is a bit too much&quot;, then you know for certain that there are tons of women who ARE showing ankle. </div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that all women would follow the etiquettes, but the scenes I mentioned were &quot;official occasions&quot; for the middle and upper class where you could ruin you name with that kind of clothes. Women who just showed their ankles were even compared with prostitutes. Furthermore the society was much stricter about those things than today. And under those circumstances the family of that woman or her husband wouldn't allow that behavior, because it would ruin their reputation, too. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the point is that you can't trust movies and tv shows to be historically correct. In fact it could lead you to very strange ideas about the time, if you trust them too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 07-30-2017, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}